claim.claim-text:
6. The system of claim 1, wherein:
the datastore is a database;
storing the first set of records in the datastore comprises logically storing the first set of records without making the first set of records durable in the datastore;
the iterative hierarchical processing scheme further involves:
for each iteration of the iterative hierarchical processing scheme:
for each record in the subset of records:
after processing the record using the one or more previously processed records, logically storing the record without making the record durable in the datastore; and



the one or more memories include additional program code that is executable by the one or more processors to:
after processing the second set of records, receive an indication to store the first set of records and the second set of records in the database; and
in response to the indication, durably write the first set of records and the second set of records to the database.

16. The method of claim 11, wherein:
the datastore is a database;
storing the first set of records in the datastore comprises logically storing the first set of records without making the first set of records durable in the datastore;
the iterative hierarchical processing scheme further involves:
for each iteration of the iterative hierarchical processing scheme:
for each record in the subset of records:
after processing the record using the one or more previously processed records, logically storing the record without making the record durable in the datastore; and



the method further comprises:
after processing the second set of records, receiving an indication to store the first set of records and the second set of records in the database; and
in response to the indication, durably writing the first set of records and the second set of records to the database.

26. The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 21, wherein:
the datastore is a database;
storing the first set of records in the datastore comprises logically storing the first set of records without making the first set of records durable in the datastore;
the iterative hierarchical processing scheme further involves:
for each iteration of the iterative hierarchical processing scheme:
for each record in the subset of records:
after processing the record using the one or more previously processed records, logically storing the record without making the record durable in the datastore; and



the non-transitory computer-readable medium further comprises additional program code that is executable by the one or more processors for causing the one or more processors to:
after processing the second set of records, receive an indication to store the first set of records and the second set of records in the database; and
in response to the indication, durably write the first set of records and the second set of records to the database.
